{{/*
Renders to ~/.config/zsh/secrets.zsh, mode 0600 (the `private_` prefix on the
FILENAME is what does that — do not move it up to a private_dot_config/ directory,
since two source entries mapping to ~/.config is a source-state conflict).

Sourced by dot_zshrc behind an existence guard, so its absence is harmless.

Three things about this file are deliberate (D6, D7, §5):

  * Gated on role == "work". KG is work tooling and the item lives in the work
    1Password account, so a personal machine renders this empty. chezmoi REMOVES a
    target whose template renders empty, which is the clean no-op we want — no
    stale secrets file left behind, and the work account never needs to exist there.

  * The account is passed as onepasswordRead's optional SECOND argument. Two op
    accounts are configured, so `op read` fails outright with "multiple accounts
    found" without it. There is no onepassword.account config key; this is the only
    place it can go. Coordinates come from .chezmoidata.toml.

  * `lookPath "op"` only proves the BINARY exists — it says nothing about the vault
    being unlocked. If op is installed but locked, onepasswordRead fails, and
    because a template error aborts target-state computation the WHOLE apply fails,
    not just this file. onepassword.prompt = false in the config makes that a
    legible error rather than a hang. Applies are expected to be interactive.

    That "rather than a hang" holds for a LOCKED VAULT only (verified 2026-08-07:
    locked, `op whoami` errors and exits 1 in about a second). It does not hold in a
    session driven by a remote client, where macOS app-data consent makes op block
    in open() forever on 1Password's group container and takes every chezmoi command
    down with it — this file is the one that triggers it. See "When chezmoi status
    hangs, suspect macOS, not chezmoi" in AGENTS.md.

The secret is fetched at APPLY time and written to disk, not read at shell startup.
So the shell pays no 1Password cost, but the plaintext does sit at 0600 between
applies, and rotating the value in 1Password requires `chezmoi apply` to propagate.
*/ -}}
{{- if and (eq .role "work") (lookPath "op") -}}
#
# Machine-local secrets. GENERATED BY CHEZMOI — do not edit; edit the template.
# Source: op://{{ .onepassword.vault }}/{{ .onepassword.kgApiItem }} in {{ .onepassword.account }}
#
export KG_API_KEY={{ onepasswordRead (printf "op://%s/%s/credential" .onepassword.vault .onepassword.kgApiItem) .onepassword.account | quote }}
{{ end -}}
